 stop you getting lost that I  discovered about a week ago so really  useful another thing you might have  noticed on your chalice dungeon  adventures are the Knights wearing plate  since there are no plate wearing Knights  in blood-borne overworld it makes you  wonder what era these Knights were from  in my head Canon may be the first forays  down into the  dungeons were from a time long ago when  plait was still popular and then finally  when they discovered what they were up  against the more experienced phrase down  into the chalice dungeons would have had  the lightweight attire that gurmann used  as a hunter hunting the beasts because  it says in his item description that he  popularized it go through enough rooms  and eventually you'll find one with a  giant bell in it and of course you're  going to ring this thing right you have  to how could you not it's a mistake when  you do what seems like every enemy in  the bloody chalice dungeon will come to  find you and murder you one of the most  interesting things with this Bell is  that you can actually use the music box  item anywhere near the Bell and the Bell  will resonate as if it was hit I've been  trying this music box on everything  lately  eldritch super hidden meanings aside I  guess what's happening here is the Bell  is set as an interactive element of the  world and that the music box checks  everything in its vicinity to elicit a  response from it and I guess that  triggers the Bell and that's exactly  what makes the music box interesting it  actually has more effects than you would  have first thought everyone knows that  Gascoigne reacts to the music box in the  boss fight since it reminds him of his  wife and daughters but did you know that  he also chuckles when you first play at  near him while he's summoned the song  itself is the first few notes of mogo's  lullaby which plays during the wet-nurse  fight what's sort of interesting is that  sometimes if you spam this music box in  this fight it gets the boss caught in  this endless cycle of sidestepping which  is really curious I read about this on  the wiki and I had to give it a go maybe  it's reacting to the tune so far as I  know it's the only creature that does  this sometimes I do wonder if it's a bug  though similar to with the giant Bell  the idea that NPCs react to things that  you do other than attacks and talking is  something I hope they put into future  games take the doll for example a lot of  you probably realized that she responds  to gestures there's no great discovery  here  she'll clap with you when you're excited  she bells back at you and  tilts her head quizzically when you do  something weird it's so endearing my  favorite is when you do the make contact  gesture and this is the gesture that's  used as some sort of communication with  the great ones wait a minute and when  your character switches sides she all of  a sudden decides to clap  maybe she's impressed that you can do it  correctly and it turns out doing it  correctly matters if you make contact  with the brain of mensis until your arms  switch sides  then you get the fully upgraded moon  room which is the one that gives you  more blood echoes and this is the room  that also mentions that the great ones  are sympathetic in spirit which is  appropriate the nightmare of menses  building is one of those places that's  able to be seen from the nightmare  frontier and I love little details like  these it makes you feel a little bit  like you're exploring a real world  blood-borne does it fairly convincingly  other areas I've noticed are that castle  cainhurst can be seen from hemic channel  Lane and you can also see the  observatory at Bergen worth from the  Forbidden Forest are there any are  missing you can let me know in the  comments I probably am missing some the  tenth little insight is to do with the B  straw just like all the force spells in  previous games B straw deflects  projectiles whether it be giant boulders  fireballs bullets you name it just draw  them away number 11 did you know that  there's a hidden exit when you're riding  up the cathedral Ward elevator I didn't  until recently it leads to the top floor  of Cathedral Ward which houses the  formless oedon rune and the urn costume  for the messengers it also lets you do  this number 12 takes us to the abandoned  hunters workshop if you position  yourself here you hear something strange  it's the sound of an old woman laughing  repeating the same sound over and over  again we've actually tracked down this  sound to a door in an alleyway in  Cathedral Ward  Oh deepest widest gratitude yes and it's  a bizarre glitch to say the least it's  so weird that a voice file would just  start playing here and it's especially  weird because this is a voice file  that's located at the end of one  characters line of dialogue and it's not  the full voice file it's very strange  but sometimes in blood-borne things are  in the game without too much purpose  take the ring of betrothal item for  example you find it in d2 marui hill  roots chalice dungeon and you can use it  to propose to analyse the vile blood  queen even with all the hard work that  you do for her you still get rejected  and it turns out you're doing some  pretty gross stuff for her Annalise  enlists hunters who go out and hunt  other hunters so you can get their blood  Drake's and feed them to your queen and  she consumes these so that she can and I  quote one day bear a child of blood but  have you ever looked closely at what the  blood dregs are when you do it makes  sense why they might help her bear a  child of blood they're clearly meant to  resemble the sperm maybe in the DLC  there will be a use for that ring but so  far there's nothing that's been found  another item like this is the yharnam  stone which you get when you kill Queen  yharnam in the chalice dungeon it reads  the Queen lies dead but her horrific  consciousness is only asleep and it  stirs in unsettling motions the yharnam  stone implies that the Queen lives on  whether inside this stone or in the  Nightmare Realm perhaps it reminds me  entirely of an Elise queen of the  vilebloods since she's the only other  character who is immortal and she's  capable of living on in a lump of flesh  and making a mistake there are actually  a lot of connections between these two  characters  I was really excited about this when I  discovered it around the time I was  doing the cainhurst lore video but none  of this information really fit in that  video because it does take a while to  explain but bear with me even the song  that plays during the arms bus fight is  titled queen of the vilebloods  which is the same song that plays when  you fight ligarius who guards the actual  queen of the vilebloods  so let's list some of the connections  there are two undying Queens who leave  behind a bloody token of their  immortality these are two queens that  share the queen of the vilebloods  soundtrack there are also two queens  with strong connections to blood one of  them started a line of followers who  partook of her blood that's Annalise and  the other one wields a kind of blood  sorcery when she fights both of them are  also related to the ring of betrothal  which is a ring found in tomorrow a hill  which is also Queen yharnam chalice  dungeon and the description of the ring  clearly relates to Queen Yanam and Queen  Anne Elise is the only character who  recognizes this ring as a wedding ring a  wedding ring that says it's only  permitted to those who are slated to  bear a special child which is a phrase  that applies to both Queens so I just  rambled on quickly about their  similarities but what does this mean  what are some of the consequences for  blood borns timeline for example well  foul blood as mentioned by alfred was  another strain of the old blood stolen  from Bergen worth long ago by a scholar  and this was likely back when the  scholars were still exploring the tombs  it makes you wonder could Queen yharnam  be the source of this file blood the  thing that seals it for me is the fact  that Queen yharnam of the chalice  dungeons has chains around her wrists  implying that she was perhaps found and  restrained at some point and maybe even  exploited so that the blood could be  taken from her and it could have got  into the populace and eventually led to  the rise of the Val bloodline also  finally when you hit Queen yharnam the  baby mojo screams out she's clearly had  something ripped  from her pregnant stomach perhaps it was  the umbilical cord that granted menses  audience with mergo the infant great one  at the top of the nightmare of menses  this would also explain Queenie Ana's  presence outside after all there are  just so many connections here between  Queenie Onam and the outside world so  I'm curious to see what you guys think  maybe we can take this a little bit  further even and I think this is all I  can think of I don't think I'll be able  to scrape together another 15 things  that are high enough in quality to  include so thanks so much for supporting  this series and I hope you stay tuned  for more blood-borne and Dark Souls 3  stuff in the future and I'll see you in  the next one cheers guys
 

